bibit-agenthub-plugin (0.3.8) resolute-porting; urgency=medium

  * Read block scalar frontmatter and stop warning about Powers the APM
    manifest already manages. Two real Skills on the board (k3-media-pipeline,
    vpu-benchmark) write their description as a folded block scalar
    (`description: >-`), whose value lives on the following indented lines. The
    custom-resource scanner only understood inline scalars, so it read an empty
    description and rejected both directories as invalid-authority-file, which
    the page then reported as "does not meet the minimum format". The scanner now
    parses `|` and `>` headers (with their chomping/indentation indicators), folds
    `>` into space-joined lines with a newline per paragraph, keeps `|` literal,
    and lets sibling keys after the block survive; the Dev Host scanner mirrors
    it so both agree on what is listed. Separately, a skip is no longer reported
    as a warning when the APM manifest already manages that (type,name): the card
    for such a Power is fed by the manifest, so re-scanning its directory only
    ever produced noise about a Power that is listed correctly.

 -- liangjunzhao <junzhao.liang@spacemit.com>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:55:00 +0800

bibit-agenthub-plugin (0.3.7) resolute-porting; urgency=medium

  * Confirm an uninstall before running it, and return to the Hub list once it
    is confirmed gone. Uninstalling is destructive, so the dialog footer now
    arms an in-dialog confirmation naming agent/type/name, exactly like the
    custom-resource delete; Cancel backs out without a request. After the write
    reconciles, the page closes the dialog when the Power is confirmed removed
    -- including the case where apm reported a non-zero exit but the reconciled
    list already shows the Power gone, since the state the user asked for is
    true and staying on the dialog would hide the reinstall entry point. A failed
    uninstall, a still-installed record, or a reconcile that could not run all
    keep the dialog open with its reason. Installing is unchanged: it still
    submits on one click and keeps its dialog.

 -- liangjunzhao <junzhao.liang@spacemit.com>  Mon, 29 Sep 2026 13:00:00 +0800

bibit-agenthub-plugin (0.3.6) resolute-porting; urgency=medium

  * Return to the Hub list after deleting a hand-installed resource. The dialog
    described a Power that no longer exists, so a successful delete now closes it
    and reloads the list; a failed delete still keeps the dialog open with the
    reason, and the page returns to the first page so a removed last item cannot
    leave an empty page behind.
  * Show a hand-installed resource's declared name on its card. The scanner used
    the authority file's name only for its minimum-format check and then dropped
    it, so a resource without v2 display fields fell back to the directory it
    happens to sit in. The declared name is now projected into name_en when the
    resource declares none (skill/plugin use name, agent uses agent.name), so a V1
    card shows what its author named it; name_zh still wins on a Chinese host and a
    declared name_en is never overridden. The directory stays the identity used for
    de-duplication and for upload/delete targets.
  * Move the APC credential into the Agent Hub page. The plugin no longer
    declares a settings contribution, so Bibit's Settings submenu has no Agent
    Hub entry; the page's first-level tabs are now My Powers / Power market /
    Settings, and the Settings tab holds the APC API Key field, its configured
    state and the clear action. settings.get.v1 and settings.update.v1 are
    unchanged: the panel still round-trips showExperimental/refreshMinutes, which
    have no consumer.

 -- liangjunzhao <junzhao.liang@spacemit.com>  Mon, 29 Sep 2026 11:00:00 +0800

bibit-agenthub-plugin (0.3.4) resolute-porting; urgency=medium

  * Show hand-installed resources next to the APM manifest. "My Powers" now
    also lists resources a user placed in an Agent's own directory tree
    (~/.bianbu-agent for bibit, ~/.codex, ~/.claude, ~/.hermes). The scan reads
    the mainstream minimum of each type only (a skill needs name+description in
    its frontmatter, a plugin a name in its manifest, an agent agent.name), so
    v1 and v2 resources both show; anything below that is reported as a warning
    instead of being dropped silently. Custom cards carry a Custom badge and a
    dashed accent, and the version slot becomes a static label because a
    hand-installed resource is a single directory.
  * Upload a custom resource to APC and delete it locally from the card dialog,
    alongside Install/Uninstall. The dialog grows a publish-message field and a
    confirm step; upload runs `apm validate` then `apm submit` (so it still
    requires Power format v2) and delete removes the local directory.
  * Store the APC API key in Agent Hub settings. The provider persists it in
    settings.json (0700 directory, 0600 file, atomic write, symlink writes
    refused) and only ever returns hasApiKey; the key reaches apm through the
    APC_API_KEY environment variable and is redacted from any reported failure.
  * New provider operations powers.custom.list.v1, powers.upload.v1,
    powers.delete.v1, settings.get.v1 and settings.update.v1; the Registry
    declares settings.update.v1's apiKey as a credential parameter, and the
    plugin's capability grant gains the three custom-resource operations.
  * Requests never carry paths: (agent,type,name[,message]) is re-resolved and
    re-validated inside the provider, and a failed custom scan degrades to one
    warning so the installed page keeps working against an older CLI.

 -- liangjunzhao <junzhao.liang@spacemit.com>  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 23:30:00 +0800

bibit-agenthub-plugin (0.3.3) resolute-porting; urgency=medium

  * Follow the host language for Power display information. Power resource
    format v2 adds display-only name_zh/name_en/description_zh; the cards and
    the details dialog now show the Chinese name and description on a Chinese
    host and the English name on an English host, instead of always showing
    the canonical call name.
  * Stay compatible with v1 records: a missing display field falls back
    (zh: name_zh, name_en, name; en: name_en, name) and the description falls
    back to the source description, so existing resources render as before.
  * The display fields are parsed when apm list --json or the APC catalog
    start emitting them; neither does yet, so this release only makes the
    receiving side ready. Power identity, requests and cache keys keep using
    the canonical name.

 -- liangjunzhao <junzhao.liang@spacemit.com>  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:20:00 +0800

bibit-agenthub-plugin (0.3.2) resolute-porting; urgency=medium

  * Fix a spurious "Power catalog request was cancelled" error in the Power
    market. Cancellation means "superseded" or "provider session torn down",
    not a user action, so it is now retryable and can no longer dead-end the
    page without a way out.
  * A market read that started before a newer one committed now answers from
    that newer catalog instead of reporting the supersede as a cancellation.
  * Regaining window focus no longer aborts and re-issues an in-flight read;
    it only refreshes once the view is idle.

